    {
      "id": "DCP-02",
      "chapter": "global",
      "anchor": "global-deep-iteration",
      "title": "Iteration of the cuspidal estimate gains twelve powers per dimension",
      "statement": "With N=n²f and at order 8qN, the radius gain in the squared estimate is τ^(16N). The local evaluation contributes τ^(−4N), leaving τ^(12N). At τ<X^(−11q), the full scalar factor is at most exp(−N)/(g^(2N)X^N).",
      "hypotheses": "The indefinite counting hypotheses give 8≤n, q≥1, q²≤n, nonempty real places, and a compatible family of isometric cuspidal vectors. The orbit cover, derivative bounds and Sobolev evaluation hold at the stated level and gap.",
